 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the county of Nassau to alienate and sell parklands to the\nColeman Country Day Camp and Coleson Properties, LLC ;.us on;",
    "basePrintNo": "S6371",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6371-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6371\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act authorizing the county of Nassau to alienate\nand sell parklands to the Coleman Country Day Camp and Coleson Proper-\nties, LLC  \n\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTHIS BILL AUTHORIZES NASSAU COUNTY TO CONVEY A PARCEL OF THE ROOSEVELT\nSOUTH PRESERVE TO THE COLEMAN COUNTRY DAY CAMP.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSECTION 1. AUTHORIZES THE COUNTY OF NASSAU TO CONVEY CERTAIN PARKLAND TO\nCOLEMAN COUNTRY DAY CAMP.\n\nSECTION 2. PROVIDES THAT THE COUNTY MAY ONLY APPROVE THE TRANSFER OF\nLAND IF THERE IS AN EQUIVALENT INVESTMENT IN ADDITIONAL PARKLAND OR\nCAPITAL PROJECTS TO EXISTING PARKS.\n\nSECTION 3. DESCRIBES THE BOUNDARIES OF THE PARCEL TO BE TRANSFERRED.\n\nSECTION 4. PROVIDES THAT THE DISCONTINUANCE OF PARKLAND SHALL NOT OCCUR\nUNTIL THE COUNTY HAS COMPLIED WITH ALL FEDERAL REQUIREMENTS PERTAINING\nTO THE CONVERSION OF PARKLAND.\n\nSECTION 5. IS THE ENACTING CLAUSE.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTHE COLEMAN COUNTRY DAY CAMP IN ROOSEVELT IS IN THE PROCESS OF FORMALLY\nACQUIRING A PARCEL OF LAND THAT HAS BEEN IN USE AS AN ACCESSORY TO THE\nCAMP FOR OVER 35 YEARS. THE PARCEL IN QUESTION IS A 3.86-ACRE SECTION OF\nTHE 73-ACRE ROOSEVELT SOUTH PRESERVE OWNED BY THE COUNTY OF NASSAU ABUT-\nTING THE CAMP. RESPONSIBLE USE AND STEWARDSHIP OF THIS LAND BY PRIVATE\nCAMP ENTITIES BEGAN IN 1972 WHEN THE COUNTY ISSUED A USE AND OCCUPANCY\nPERMIT TO CAMP COUNTRY DAY CAMP'S PREDECESSOR, CAMP BAUMANN, TO USE A\nPORTION OF THE PRESERVE FOR LAND BEAUTIFICATION, AN ECOLOGICAL NATURE\nSTUDY, AND FOR OTHER SOCIAL, RECREATIONAL AND EDUCATIONAL PURPOSES. IN\n1985, THE COUNTY REISSUED A USE AND OCCUPANCY PERMIT TO COLEMAN COUNTRY\nDAY CAMP FOR SIMILAR EDUCATIONAL PURPOSES, WHICH HAS BEEN EXTENDED\nTHROUGH 2022.\n\nTHE COLEMAN COUNTRY DAY CAMP HAS AGREED TO INCLUDE COVENANTS IN THE DEED\nTHAT THE PROPERTY \"SHALL BE FOREVER USED FOR RECREATIONAL USES AND OTHER\nCAMPING-RELATED USES AND OTHER ACTIVITIES RELATED TO THE OPERATION OF A\nSUMMER CAMP AND YEAR-ROUND SCHOOL ACTIVITIES.\" FOLLOWING A COMMUNITY\nMEETING ON THE PROPOSED SALE, THE COUNTY PLANNING COMMISSION APPROVED\nTHE SALE AND IN SEPTEMBER 2009 THE COUNTY LEGISLATURE APPROVED THE\nRESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE SALE.\n\nTHE CAMP AND COUNTY HAVE PERFORMED ALL DUE DILIGENCE TO ENSURE THAT THE\nSALE WILL BE OF GREAT BENEFIT TO THE LOCAL COMMUNITY. THIS BILL WILL\nALLOW THE SALE TO PROCEED WITHOUT FURTHER HINDRANCE.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNONE TO THE STATE.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nTHIS ACT SHALL TAKE EFFECT IMMEDIATELY AFTER IT SHALL HAVE BECOME LAW.\n",
