    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6371a\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the county of Nassau to alienate and sell parklands\nto the Coleman Country Day Camp and Coleson Properties, LLC  \n\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTHE PURPOSE OF THIS BILL IS TO CONVEY A PARCEL OF THE ROOSEVELT SOUTH\nPRESERVE TO THE COLEMAN COUNTRY DAY CAMP.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSECTION 1. AUTHORIZES NASSAU COUNTY TO CONVEY CERTAIN PARKLAND TO COLE-\nMAN COUNTRY DAY CAMP.\n\nSECTION 2. PROVIDES THAT THE COUNTY MAY ONLY APPROVE THE PARKLAND TRANS-\nFER IF AN AMOUNT EQUIVALENT TO THE LAND'S FAIR MARKET VALUE IS USED FOR\nTHE PURCHASE OF ADDITIONAL PARKLAND OR FOR CAPITAL PROJECTS TO EXISTING\nPARKS.\n\nSECTION 3. DESCRIBES THE BOUNDARIES OF THE PARCEL TO BE TRANSFERRED.\n\nSECTION 4. PROVIDES THAT THE DISCONTINUANCE OF PARKLAND SHALL NOT OCCUR\nUNTIL THE COUNTY HAS COMPLIED WITH ALL FEDERAL REQUIREMENTS PERTAINING\nTO THE CONVERSION OF PARKLAND.\n\nSECTION 5. IS THE ENACTING CLAUSE\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTHE COLEMAN COUNTRY DAY CAMP IN ROOSEVELT IS INTERESTED IN FORMALLY\nACQUIRING A PARCEL OF LAND THAT HAS BEEN IN USE AS AN ACCESSORY TO THE\nCAMP FOR OVER 35 YEARS. THE PARCEL IN QUESTION IS A 3.86-ACRE SECTION OF\nTHE 73-ACRE ROOSEVELT SOUTH PRESERVE OWNED BY THE COUNTY OF NASSAU ABUT-\nTING THE CAMP. RESPONSIBLE USE AND STEWARDSHIP OF THIS LAND BY PRIVATE\nCAMP ENTITIES BEGAN IN 1972 WHEN THE COUNTY ISSUED A USE AND OCCUPANCY\nPERMIT TO CAMP COUNTRY DAY CAMP'S PREDECESSOR, CAMP BAUMANN, TO USE A\nPORTION OF THE PRESERVE FOR LAND BEAUTIFICATION, AN ECOLOGICAL NATURE\nSTUDY, AND FOR OTHER SOCIAL, RECREATIONAL AND EDUCATIONAL PURPOSES. IN\n1985, THE COUNTY RE-ISSUED A USE AND OCCUPANCY PERMIT TO COLEMAN COUNTRY\nDAY CAMP FOR SIMILAR EDUCATIONAL PURPOSES, WHICH HAS BEEN EXTENDED\nTHROUGH 2022. THE COLEMAN COUNTRY DAY CAMP HAS AGREED TO INCLUDE COVEN-\nANTS IN THE DEED THAT THE PROPERTY \"SHALL BE FOREVER USED FOR RECRE-\nATIONAL USES AND OTHER CAMPING-RELATED USES AND OTHER ACTIVITIES RELATED\nTO THE OPERATION OF A SUMMER CAMP AND YEAR-ROUND SCHOOL ACTIVITIES.\"\n\nFOLLOWING A COMMUNITY MEETING ON THE PROPOSED SALE, THE COUNTY PLANNING\nCOMMISSION APPROVED THE SALE AND IN SEPTEMBER 2009 THE COUNTY LEGISLA-\nTURE APPROVED THE RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE SALE. THE CAMP AND COUNTY\nHAVE PERFORMED ALL DUE DILIGENCE TO ENSURE THAT THE SALE WILL BE OF\nGREAT BENEFIT TO THE LOCAL COMMUNITY. THIS BILL WILL ALLOW THE SALE TO\nPROCEED WITHOUT FURTHER HINDRANCE.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNONE\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nTHIS ACT SHALL TAKE EFFECT IMMEDIATELY.\n",
